# Round-six setup, part 9: `SetupNeed6`

The procedure is `startP` (frozen: `n` and `b = lg n`), the compiled register program `setRS`,
and `oP` (frozen: `2^{2n}` on `rO`). Its cost is `O(n) + cSet · kU`; the second term is
`O(d r² p²) ≤ T p` for large `n` (since `T ≥ r³/4` once `d ≥ 3`, and `r = 2^ℓ` beats every fixed
power of `b`).
